   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Who you are and where you come from",
     "texto": [
      "The verb **ser** is used for three very useful things: to say your name, to say where you are from and to say what you do for a living.\n\nFor origin you use **ser + de**:\n\n- **Soy de Londres.**\n- **Soy de España.**\n\nNotice that no article is needed: «de España», not «de la España».\n\nFor nationality, the adjective changes with the person: **español** if it's a man, **española** if it's a woman.\n\nAnd for your job you don't need an article either: **Soy profesora**, not «soy una profesora»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "The verb ser and the article you don't need",
     "texto": [
      "The verb **ser** in the present tense is conjugated like this:\n\n- yo **soy**\n- tú **eres**\n- él / ella / usted **es**\n- nosotros **somos**\n- vosotros **sois**\n- ellos **son**\n\nAnd here's a rule that surprises people: **no article goes before a profession**. In Spanish you say «soy profesor», not «soy un profesor».\n\nThe same happens with origin: «soy de México», never «soy del México»."
     ],
